<title>ITALY: Olivetti shares rise, trigger suspension.</title>
<headline>Olivetti shares rise, trigger suspension.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in troubled information technology group Olivetti triggered automatic suspension on the Milan stock market by rising to touch a 10 percent fluctuation limit.</p>
<p>The stock last traded at 511.5 lire per share on Wednesday after hitting a fresh record low of 465 lire in spasmodic trade on Tuesday, when it repeatedly triggered suspension for falling to touch the 10 percent floor.</p>
<p>The stock market council said trading in shares would try to resume at 1200 GMT.</p>
</text>
